ower angle: (002) to about 18.6\u00b0, (101) to about 25.3\u00b0 as the strongest line, (011) to about 32.5\u00b0, and (103) to about 36.9\u00b0.\n- These line up with the observed peaks, and no leftover peak needs a second phase.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-760590\"], \"confidence\": 0.6, \"note\": \"Strongest peak at 25.3\u00b0 with 18.6\u00b0 and 32.5\u00b0 matches an expanded Li2CuO2-type pattern (Li5Cu3O6); the spinel and perovskite candidates lack their characteristic strong reflections.\"}",
